  "priorExpiration": "2003-12-21",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 5102.68 Pemigewasset River.\n\n(a) No person shall operate a motorboat at a speed exceeding 10 miles per hour on the Pemigewasset River between Ayer’s Island Dam in the town of Bristol and the bridge that crosses the river from Plymouth to Holderness.\n\n(b) No person shall operate a seaplane on the Pemigewasset River from the Route 104 bridge north to Sawhegenet Falls in New Hampton.\n\nSource. #2351, eff 4-25-83; ss by #3010, eff 5-2-85; ss by #4562, eff 1-3-89; ss by #5936, INTERIM, eff 1-3-95, EXPIRES: 5-3-95 (formerly Saf-C 402.59); ss by #6005, eff 3-24-95, EXPIRED: 3-24-03\n\nNew. #7904, INTERIM, eff 6-24-03, EXPIRED: 12-21-03\n\nNew. #8172, eff 9-21-04 (from Saf-C 402.53); ss by #10169, EXEMPT, eff 8-8-12 (formerly Saf-C 402.61) (See Revision Note #2 at Chapter Heading for Saf-C 5100)",
